Package: mica-busybox
Version: 1.38.0-mica1
Source-Date-Epoch: 1792383800
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Mica OS <hi@micaos.dev>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Description: BusyBox binary for diagnostics, its applets a fallback in PATH
 /usr/bin/busybox: the upstream BusyBox release compiled statically for this
 architecture, so it runs with none of the root's libraries. One link per applet
 under /usr/libexec/busybox, which /etc/profile.d/mica-busybox.sh puts last in a
 login shell's PATH: an applet answers to its plain name (ping, vi) only where the
 root ships no command of that name.
